[line]
[size=4]What is NOT changed[/size]
[list]
[*][b]No spell balance changes, with one deliberate exception.[/b] Damage, magicka cost, duration and cooldowns are all Enai's, untouched. Enderal keeps all five of Skyrim's magic skills and only renames them, so Apocalypse's spells scale off your Elementalism, Entropy, Light Magic, Mentalism and Psionics without any conversion at all. The exception is Arcane Fever on the 19 self-heals (see above) — that is not a rebalance of Enai's numbers but the addition of a cost that only exists in Enderal, and without it those spells bypass the game's central survival mechanic entirely.[/*]
[*][b]No new spells, no removed records.[/b] The fifteen cut summons are still in Apocalypse; they are simply never handed to you.[/*]
[*][b]No Enderal records rewritten.[/b] The nine leveled lists are appended to, never edited.[/*]
[/list]
For reference, in case you have wondered which Enderal skill governs an Apocalypse spell:

[code]
  Skyrim school     Enderal discipline    Higher school
  Destruction       Elementalism          (its own art)
  Conjuration       Entropy               Sinistra
  Restoration       Light Magic           Thaumaturgy
  Alteration        Mentalism             Thaumaturgy
  Illusion          Psionics              Sinistra[/code]

Note the last two — Alteration is [i]Mentalism[/i] and Illusion is [i]Psionics[/i], not the pairing you would guess.
[line]
[size=4]Compatibility and load order[/size]

This [b]is[/b] [font=Courier New]Apocalypse - Magic of Skyrim.esp[/font] — it takes the original's place in your load order, exactly where that plugin already sat. It is a full ESP, not ESL-flagged, because it carries all ~3,900 of Apocalypse's own records.

Beyond Apocalypse's own records it touches [b]eleven[/b] Enderal records:
[list]
[*][b]Six merchant chests[/b] — [font=Courier New]CCFunkentanz[/font], [font=Courier New]STTurious[/font], [font=Courier New]UC_Barnabas[/font], [font=Courier New]CCSteinschlag[/font], [font=Courier New]MaxusTabbakus02[/font], [font=Courier New]CCMilbert[/font] — each gains its tier of spell tomes[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]_00E_SpellBooksLootA[/font] through [font=Courier New]D[/font] — the spellbook loot tiers[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]00E_ScrollsLowChance[/font] — the scroll loot pool[/*]
[/list]
If another mod edits those same records, the later plugin wins outright and one mod's additions are lost — either order them accordingly or merge with a Bashed/Smashed patch, as with any leveled list or container conflict.

[b]Known conflict — KataPUMB Spell Package.[/b] That mod adds the same 15 staves to three of Enderal's spell merchants: Emberlord and Fireflash, Torius Flameling and Tarhutie in Riverville. This mod claims the first two, so [b]those staves are no longer sold there[/b]. Tarhutie is deliberately left alone for exactly this reason — the staff set is identical at all three shops, so all 15 remain buyable from him, and nothing of KataPUMB's becomes unobtainable. That is also why the Apprentice tier sits with Maxus Tabbakus in Duneville rather than Tarhutie, whose gold is near-identical.

[b]Compatibility patches planned.[/b] Dedicated patches for [b]KataPUMB Spell Package[/b] and [b]Enderal Gameplay Overhaul (EGO)[/b] are on the way as separate downloads. Neither exists yet — until they do, the KataPUMB note above describes the current behaviour, and EGO is untested against this.

[b]Pinned to Apocalypse 10.2.3.[/b] This ships a rebuilt copy of that exact version's plugin. A newer Apocalypse must not be used with it — install 10.2.3, or wait for this to be refreshed.
[line]
[size=4]Known limitations[/size]
[list]
[*][b]The 67 staves are unobtainable.[/b] Deliberate — see above. If you want them, the console still works.[/*]
[*][b]Banish Living has no visual effect[/b], and a couple of spells that would have spoken a line stay silent. Both are Apocalypse pointing at vanilla Skyrim records Enderal does not have. They are cosmetic, and inventing replacements would have meant guessing at Enai's intent, so they were left alone and written down instead.[/*]
[*][b]Scroll inventory previews and one summoned sword's first-person model are missing[/b] — Apocalypse points all 144 scrolls at a vanilla display model Enderal lacks. That reference is left exactly as Enai wrote it, so all 144 behave identically instead of a handful being quietly different.[/*]
[*][b]The Nightmare ground sigil may show the wrong particle effect.[/b] Its addon node index collided with one of Enderal's own effects, which would have replaced an Enderal visual with Apocalypse's. The conflict is resolved in Enderal's favour — protecting the base game — which leaves Apocalypse's mesh looking for a node that has moved. Fixing it properly needs an edited mesh, and this release ships no assets.[/*]
[*][b]Spell tome tiering is by rank name, not by playtested power.[/b] Which merchant sells a spell follows its Apocalypse rank, not a measurement against Enderal's difficulty curve. Feedback welcome.[/*]
[*][b]Erodan's Embrace costs a flat 20 Arcane Fever.[/b] Every other heal is priced off the exact number of points it restores, but that one is scripted to heal you to full — there is no number in the record to price, so 20 assumes a late-game health pool. If it feels wrong at your level, say so.[/*]
[*][b]Merchant inventories get long.[/b] Emberlord and Fireflash goes from 96 entries to 141. SkyUI's category filter handles it, but it is a visibly fuller shop than the base game's.[/*]
[*][b]Tome names carry no "(Rank N)" suffix[/b], unlike most of Enderal's. That is intentional: in Enderal that suffix means the same spell exists at another strength, gated on player level, and Apocalypse spells have exactly one version each. Enderal leaves 13 of its own single-strength tomes unsuffixed for the same reason.[/*]
[*][b]Requires Enderal SE[/b], which is pinned to Skyrim SE [b]1.5.97[/b]. This is a plugin only, so no SKSE version concerns apply to it.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=4]Credits[/size]

[b]Enai Siaion[/b] — Apocalypse: every one of the 373 spells, all the design, and every asset. [b]This release is his plugin, modified.[/b] It contains no assets, no spells and no ideas of its own; it exists so his work reaches you in a different game. Redistributed under the mod's stated permissions, which allow modification and re-upload with credit. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/1090]Go and endorse the original[/url] — you need it installed anyway.
[b]SureAI[/b] — Enderal: Forgotten Stories, and the written lore every replacement name was taken from.
